  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s011-p00129",
      "source_en": "Recently it has been noticed that amongst the Bubaline engravings representing wild fauna there are figures of domesticated cattle with the same dark patina, of the same style and engraved in the same sites, often side by side. For this reason some scholars (Muzzolini 1995a, b; Le Quellec 2006b) consider that both the Bubaline and the Pastoral are a single unique style belonging to the Pastoral period during which images of both wild and domesticated animals were engraved by herders.",
